.TH HTTPCLIENT 2
.SH NAME
httpclient: Hdr, Resp, init, get, post, request \- HTTP/1.1 client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "httpclient.m";
http := load Httpclient Httpclient->PATH;

Hdr: adt {
	name:	string;
	val:	string;
};

Resp: adt {
	code:	int;
	reason:	string;
	hdrs:	list of Hdr;
	body:	array of byte;

	hdr:	fn(r: self ref Resp, name: string): string;
};

init:		fn(): string;
get:		fn(url: string, hdrs: list of Hdr): (ref Resp, string);
post:		fn(url: string, hdrs: list of Hdr, body: array of byte): (ref Resp, string);
request:	fn(method: string, url: string, hdrs: list of Hdr,
			body: array of byte): (ref Resp, string);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Httpclient
makes an HTTP/1.1 request and returns the reply.
.PP
.B Init
must be called first and returns nil, or a diagnostic if a module it
needs will not load.
.PP
.BR Get ,
.B post
and
.B request
each return a
.B Resp
and a nil error string, or nil and a diagnostic.  A reply that is not
200 is not an error: the status is in
.BR Resp.code ,
and it is for the caller to decide.
.PP
.B Resp.hdr
looks up a reply header by name, case-insensitively as the protocol
requires, and returns nil if it is absent.
.PP
Every request is sent with
.BR "Connection: close" .
That costs a connection per request and in exchange removes every
question about where one reply ends and the next begins.  Replies are
read with a
.BR Content-Length ,
as
.B chunked
transfer-encoding, or to end of file, in that order of preference.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/httpclient.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR hget (1),
.IR cloudfs (4),
.IR url (2),
.IR dial (2)
.SH BUGS
Plain HTTP only: there is no TLS on this branch.  For a metadata
service on a link-local address that is not a limitation, because the
request never leaves the hypervisor; for anything else it is.
.PP
There is no redirect following, no authentication, and no connection
reuse.
